  "id": "structural-model",
  "term": "structural model",
  "definition": "In this context, a structural model is an integrated framework that links several psychological factors so they can jointly explain a behavior and its outcomes. Here, it refers to combining personality, affect, and work attitudes to account for quiet quitting and related behaviors.",
